The script flash-linux.sh allows flashing raw (WIC) images onto a device via
a USB connection. It is meant to be executed on a host computer running a
GNU/Linux distro. The communication with the device initially uses the SDP
protocol for loading a special version of U-Boot which in turn provides
flashing capabilities via the Fastboot protocol.

If the script does not work out of the box, you might have to manually
install the appropriate libraries.

For a Debian based distro, run the following command:

$ sudo apt install libudev1 libusb-1.0-0

To learn how to use the script, execute:

$ ./flash-linux.sh --help
